Headline: Beyond the numbers: What really decided who survived the Titanic? 🚢

I just wrapped up a mini-EDA on the classic Titanic dataset, and the results go deeper than just "gender and class." 
By cleaning the data and engineering new features like Family Size, some fascinating patterns emerged.

Key takeaways from my analysis:
Family Matters: Having a small family on board actually increased survival rates compared to traveling alone or with a very large group.
Age Gaps: Visualizing the age distribution helped identify which demographics were prioritized during the rescue.
Data Integrity: Improved my workflow by implementing mean imputation for missing values and streamlining the dataset for better model readiness. 
Data isn't just about rows and columns; it’s about the stories hidden within. Check out my visualizations below! 📊
